Description:

JMAP method calls now always require an accountId, as RFC 8620 Section 3.6.2
says.  A call other than Core/echo that omits accountId, or gives a null or
non-string one, is rejected with invalidArguments.  The jmap_require_accountid
option, which made this behaviour optional, is deprecated and ignored.


Documentation:

lib/imapoptions/jmap_require_accountid


Config changes:

jmap_require_accountid (deprecated)


Upgrade instructions:

Clients must send accountId on every method call but Core/echo.  Remove
jmap_require_accountid from imapd.conf.


